From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Correct indexed subsequence newline offsets

SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

This generic correction is not a RISC-V architecture workaround. The number
of completed lines before a zero-based start is start / line_blen, and their
byte contribution includes the complete LF or CRLF width. The original
crlf.fasta fixture places chr:4 at byte 15 (G), not byte 11 (LF). Keep all
original fixtures and exercise them through an independent sequential oracle.
Remove this patch when the selected upstream release includes this correction.

--- a/Fasta.cpp
+++ b/Fasta.cpp
@@ -325 +325 @@
-    int newlines_before = start > 0 ? (start - 1) / entry.line_blen : 0;
+    int newlines_before = start / entry.line_blen;
@@ -331 +331 @@
-    fseek64(file, (off_t) (entry.offset + newlines_before + start), SEEK_SET);
+    fseek64(file, (off_t) (entry.offset + newlines_before * bytes_per_newline + start), SEEK_SET);
